{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The diagram of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true."}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Low child","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High child"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"root","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"x0","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x1","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"false"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"true","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The test of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"text":" is shared: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"},{"text":" false and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1"},{"text":" both leave ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"text":" equal to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"text":", so both lead","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the one vertex that stands for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" in O(|","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{